-- #1265: two DIFFERENT interfaces (`ifa.Speak`, `ifb.Greet`) declare a method of the
-- SAME bare name `speak` with different defaults, and ONE type (`Dog`) implements both
-- with METHOD-LESS impls.  The Core IR untagged-default registry is keyed
-- (method, tag) -- `mdk_default_speak_Dog` -- which has no room for the interface, so
-- both defaults collapse onto one symbol and first-match wins.
--
-- CORRECT ANSWER IS NOT IN DISPUTE, and was derived from the spec BEFORE the engines
-- were run: DICT-SEMANTICS §5 / §5.1 M1 -- an interface default fills the slot the
-- SELECTED INSTANCE omits.  `sayA`'s selected instance is `ifa::Speak Dog` (default
-- "A-default"); `sayB`'s is `ifb::Greet Dog` (default "B-default").  §8 I4 makes a
-- class `(module, name)`, so neither can observe the other's default.
--   CORRECT: A-default|B-default
--   ACTUAL:  A-default|A-default   (eval AND native AND wasm, exit 0, no diagnostic)
--
-- ⚠️ NO ENGINE PRODUCES THE CORRECT ANSWER IN ANY IMPORT ORDER -- see order-probe.mdk,
-- which is this file with the first two imports swapped and prints B-default|B-default.
import ca.{sayA}
import cb.{sayB}
import dog.{Dog(..)}

main : <IO> Unit
main = putStrLn (sayA Dog ++ "|" ++ sayB Dog)
